tus =pending\\n 2. Board member logs in → Dashboard → Approves user → status =approved; role=residential or board\\n 3. Approved residents gain access to protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\n 4. Board can publish News posts & edit informational pages via point-and-click editor inside Dashboard\\n\\nDATA MODEL (SQL snippets run via Supabase SQL editor)\\n```\\ncreate table profiles (\\n  id uuid primary key references auth.users on delete cascade,\\n  email text unique,\\n  role text check (role in ('resident','board')) default 'resident',\\n  status text check (status in ('pending','approved')) default 'pending',\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\n);\\n\\ncreate table pages (\\n  slug text primary key,\\n  title text,\\n  content html,\\n  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\n);\\n\\ncreate table news (\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\n  title text,\\n  content html,\\n  author uuid references profiles(id),\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\n);\\n\\ncreate table documents (\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\n  title text,\\n  category text check (category in ('dues','annual_meetings')),\\n  file_url text,\\n  uploaded_by uuid references profiles(id),\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\n);\\n```\\nRLS POLICIES (samples)\\n```\\n-- Enable row level security\\nalter table profiles enable row level security;\\ncreate policy \\\"Users view own profile\\\" on profiles\\n  for select using (auth.uid() = id);\\ncreate policy \\\"Board can view all\\\" on profiles\\n  for select using (exists (select 1 from profiles p where p.id = auth.uid() and p.role='board'));\\n-- Similar policies for update/insert on other tables.\\n```\\n\\nSTEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION\\n1. Local Setup\\n   a) Install tooling: `npm i -g vercel supabase@latest`\\n   b) `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-site --typescript --tailwind`\\n   c) `cd hoa-site && npm install @supabase/supabase-js @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit`\\n\\n2. Supabase Project\\n   a) Owner creates Supabase project in dashboard → obtain SUPABASE_URL & SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.\\n   b) Run SQL blocks above (SQL editor).\\n   c) Configure Auth → Email provider → enable Confirm via email.\\n   d) Storage: create bucket `restricted-docs` (private).\\n\\n3. Environment Variables (both locally and in Vercel)\\n   SUPABASE_URL= <project-url>\\n   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= <anon-key>\\n\\n4. Next.js Implementation\\n   • `/lib/supabaseClient.ts` – singleton init.\\n   • AuthContext provider to track user & claims (status / role from `profiles` table).\\n   • `withAuth(allowed)` HOC to guard pages; show pending approval notice if status!='approved'.\\n   • Pages & Routes\\n      - `/` Home (seasonal theme auto by month; CSS vars set in `ThemeProvider`).\\n      - `/contact`, `/bylaws`, `/schools` – public pages, editable via dashboard.\\n      - `/login` & `/signup` forms.\\n      - `/dashboard` (board only) → Tabs: Pending Approvals, Manage Pages, News, Documents.\\n      - `/dues`, `/annual-meetings`, `/news-events` – resident-only (approved).\\n   • TipTap editor component reused in Dashboard for rich-text.\\n\\n5. Board Dashboard Features\\n   a) Pending Approvals – table of profiles where status='pending'; Approve button → update status to 'approved'.\\n   b) Pages – list pages; Edit opens TipTap; Save → upsert to `pages` table.\\n   c) News – CRUD posts.\\n   d) Documents – upload to Supabase Storage bucket, create row in `documents` table.\\n\\n6. Deployment\\n   a) Push repo to GitHub.\\n   b) Connect to Vercel → Import project → set env vars.\\n   c) Add custom domain dunbaroakshoa.com in Vercel UI; update DNS A/CNAME records at registrar.\\n   d) Verify HTTPS works.\\n\\n7. Validation Checklist\\n   [ ] Public pages load.\\n   [ ] Signup email received; user in Pending list.\\n   [ ] Board approves user; resident can access protected pages.\\n   [ ] News post appears.\\n   [ ] Seasonal colors change (modify system date in 